{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions","id":1552345,"title":"Basic Splat Interactions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-13T21:43:58-07:00","id":1552345,"title":"Basic Splat Interactions","content":"I have a few questions I would like to ask, but they're not so simple and I need eleven answers: one for each splat and every splat, even if the answer is obvious. Preferably with reference to books and pages where the answers can be found.<br /> <br /> 1- <i>Do they have normal blood a Vampire can drink? If not, what do they have in its place?</i><br /> 2- <i>Do they have a human Soul? In which state is this Soul?</i><br /> 3- <i>Can their Soul, Soul-like or substitute be removed? Which rules do they follow if Soulless?</i><br /> 4- <i>Do they dream as normal? What difference is there?</i><br /> 5- <i>Can they act as Demiurges? Can they leave Ghosts behind?</i><br /> 6- <i>What would normally be the biggest challenge for a Demon using one of them as Cover?</i><br /> 7- <i>Would it be possible for their regular powers to sometimes produce a Divergence? How?</i><br /> 8 - <i>How does the splat recovers Willpower (Anchors, sleep, everything)? How frequent and hard should recovery be?</i><br /> <br /> My plan is to compile the answers in this OP for anyone's future reference:<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire</b><br /> - <u>Blood:</u> it causes addiction, Bond and transformation. It naturally satisfies a High Blood Potency Vampire;<br /> Obs.: The <i>Unnatural Affinity </i>Merit effectively makes the fluids of the target non-normal creature type to be drinkable and satisfy High BP.<br /> - <u>Soul:</u> it's harder to affect with magic than a mortal soul, but otherwise unremarkable (pending investigation on nature). Loosing it causes the Soulless Condition;<br /> - <u>Dream:</u> normal. They have an Oneiroi and connect to the Temenos and Anima Mundi as normal;<br /> - <u>Ghost:</u> it's unclear if the frequency is different from a mortal (either lower or higher), but happens;<br /> Obs.: While unlikely, the Embrace may produce a ghost. Producing a ghost doesn't affect the chances of the Embrace or other ways of becoming a Vampire.<br /> - <u>Cover:</u> a Demon passing as a Vampire will have to deal with the preternatural senses and Predatory Aura of Vampires, and is unlikely to fool them.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf</b><br /> - <u>Blood:</u> normal human blood, although the ST may decide the spiritual essence within causes a minor effect;<br /> - <u>Soul:</u> it's harder to affect with magic than a mortal soul, but otherwise unremarkable (pending investigation on nature). Loosing it causes the Soulless Condition;<br /> - <u>Dream:</u> weird. Their Oneiroi is inhuman and does not connect to the Temenos, although it does connect to the Anima Mundi;<br /> - <u>Ghost:</u> it's unclear if the frequency is different from a mortal (probably lower), but happens;<br /> - <u>Cover:</u> if fooling their senses isn't hard enough, a Demon passing as a Werewolf will struggle with traversing to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Mage</b><br /> - <u>Blood:</u> normal human blood;<br /> - <u>Soul:</u> it's harder to affect with magic than a mortal soul, but otherwise unremarkable (pending investigation on nature). Loosing it causes the Soulless Condition;<br /> - <u>Dream:</u> normal. They have an Oneiroi and connect to the Temenos and Anima Mundi as normal;<br /> - <u>Ghost:</u> it's unclear if the frequency is different from a mortal (either lower or higher), but happens;<br /> - <u>Cover:</u> a Demon can pass for a Mage as long as they avoid heavy scrutiny, but that's a loosing game in the long term.<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling</b><br /> - <u>Blood:</u> normal human blood, although the ST may decide the Arcadian influence causes a minor effect;<br /> - <u>Soul:</u> it's harder to affect with magic than a mortal soul, but otherwise unremarkable (pending investigation on nature). Loosing it causes the Soulless Condition;<br /> Obs.: it's possible that removing a Changeling's soul will turn them into a Soulless Changeling instead of inflicting the normal Soulless Condition.<br /> - <u>Dream:</u> normal. They have an Oneiroi and connect to the Temenos and Anima Mundi as normal;<br /> - <u>Ghost:</u> it's unclear if the frequency is different from a mortal (probably lower), but happens;<br /> - <u>Cover:</u> on most cases it simply won't imitate their <i>mien</i>, being obvious to other Changelings.<br /> Obs.: If the <i>mien</i> is sufficiently similar to a human being, it <i><b>may</b></i> happen that the Cover imitates it, but not the <i>Mask</i>. Regardless, it never has both.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean</b><br /> - <u>Blood:</u> have Humours instead of human blood, although a Vampire may not notice nor be inconvenienced by this;<br /> Obs.: at the ST discretion, their blood may leak some <i>Pyros</i>. In this case, it is explosively dangerous.<br /> - <u>Soul:</u> it has Azoth in it's place, which can't be affected by effects that deal with souls, being immune to the Soulless Condition;<br /> Obs.: A once-Promethean human has a normal, unremarkable soul (pending investigation on nature). Loosing it causes the Soulless Condition.<br /> - <u>Dream:</u> weird. It doesn't have an Oneiros and doesn't connect to either the Temenos or Anima Mundi, but has a connection to the Divine Fire and has the potential for <i>Elpis Visions</i>;<br /> - <u>Ghost:</u> extremely unlikely to leave a Ghost due to their overall nature, but not impossible;<br /> - <u>Cover:</u> as they lack souls, a Demon can't acquire this Cover;<br /> - <u>Demiurges:</u> any intelligent creature may act as a Demiurge and create a Promethean, as long as they do so through Alchemy. The result will probably be <i>Extempore</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter</b><br /> - <u>Blood:</u> normal human blood;<br /> Obs.: some <i>Endowments</i> may change their blood, with varying effects.<br /> - <u>Soul:</u> normal human soul, regardless of powers, Merits and <i>Endowments</i>;<br /> - <u>Dream:</u> normal. They have an Oneiroi and connect to the Temenos and Anima Mundi as normal;<br /> - <u>Ghost:</u> it's unclear if the frequency is much higher than normal, but it is at least the same as normal people;<br /> - <u>Cover:</u> it's unclear if a Cover can have some <i>Endowments</i>. Otherwise this is a feasible Cover.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<b>Geist</b><br /> - <u>Blood:</u> has unnatural blood, still fresh, but dead. It's unclear if it satisfies a normal Vampire;<br /> - <u>Soul:</u> it has the Geist in it's place, which can't be affected by effects that deal with souls, being immune to the Soulless Condition;<br /> - <u>Dream:</u> weird. It doesn't have an Oneiros and doesn't connect to either the Temenos or Anima Mundi;<br /> - <u>Ghost:</u> it's extremely unlikely that one will form during a &quot;normal&quot; death, but not impossible. It's somewhat more likely upon definitive death, but still rare;<br /> - <u>Cover:</u> as they lack souls, a Demon can't acquire this Cover.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<b>Mummy</b><br /> - <u>Blood:</u> has unnatural blood, still fresh, but dead. It's unclear if it satisfies a normal Vampire;<br /> - <u>Soul:</u> while human, their souls are the property of the Judges (or a possessing Shan'iatu) and can't be tampered with, being immune to the Soulless Condition;<br /> - <u>Dream:</u> normal. They have an Oneiroi and connect to the Temenos and Anima Mundi as normal;<br /> - <u>Ghost:</u> extremely unlikely to leave a Ghost due to their overall nature, but not impossible;<br /> - <u>Cover:</u> a Demon can't acquire their souls, and as such can't access this Cover.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon</b><br /> - <u>Blood:</u> normal human blood while under a Cover, even if the Cover is a supernatural creature;<br /> Obs.: it's unclear if the Demonic Form has blood or only <i>Aether</i>, which can't sustain a normal Vampire.<br /> Obs.2: a Vampire with adequate <i>Unnatural Affinity</i> can feed from a Demon in any form or Cover and satisfy High BP.<br /> - <u>Soul:</u> they don't have a soul or anything in its place, being immune to the Soulless Condition;<br /> Obs.: it's unclear if the Cover of a Soul Pact has the original soul. If it has, then it can be manipulated as a normal human soul;<br /> Obs.2: Spoofing soul magic will return the impression that the Demon has a normal, unremarkable soul, but that successfully resisted any attempt to tamper with;<br /> Obs.3: under some, very unusual circumstances, a Demon <b>may</b> have the Soulless Condition applied to a Cover.<br /> - <u>Dream:</u> weird. It doesn't have an Oneiros and doesn't connect to either the Temenos or Anima Mundi;<br /> - <u>Ghost:</u> extremely unlikely to leave a Ghost due to their overall nature, but not impossible;<br /> Obs.: it's unclear if such a ghost would be in Demonic Form or under the Cover of death.<br /> - <u>Cover:</u> Demons trade in Soul Contracts, but once one assumes a Cover, it can't be taken by another, and as they lack souls, a Demon can't acquire this Cover.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast</b><br /> - <u>Blood:</u> normal human blood, although the ST may decide the Horror within causes a minor effect;<br /> - <u>Soul:</u> it has the Horror in it's place, which can't be affected by effects that deal with souls, being immune to the Soulless Condition;<br /> - <u>Dream:</u> weird. The Beast fuses with the Horror to their <i>Lair</i> (or just goes to the <i>Lair</i> at <i>Satiety</i> 10). It doesn't have an Oneiros, but the <i>Lair</i> connects to the Temenos, other <i>Lairs</i> and Oneiroi in the region;<br /> Obs.: while the connection to the Anima Mundi is faint, the Beast is capable of traveling there through other innate powers, regardless.<br /> - <u>Ghost:</u> extremely unlikely to leave a Ghost due to their overall nature, but not impossible;<br /> Obs.: more common than leaving a ghost, Beasts can leave an unfettered Horror under some circumstances.<br /> - <u>Cover:</u> as they lack souls, a Demon can't acquire this Cover.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<b>Deviant</b><br /> - <u>Blood:</u> normal human blood, although the ST may decide the specific Scars and Variations cause a minor effect;<br /> Obs.: some Scars and Variations affect their blood directly, usually making it dangerous.<br /> - <u>Soul:</u> while human, their souls are too broken and can't be tampered with, being immune to the Soulless Condition;<br /> - <u>Dream:</u> normal. They have an Oneiroi and connect to the Temenos and Anima Mundi as normal;<br /> - <u>Ghost:</u> it's unclear if the frequency is different from a mortal (probably lower), but happens;<br /> - <u>Cover:</u> a Demon can't acquire their souls, and as such can't access this Cover;<br /> \u200b\u200b- <u>Divergence:</u> through either accident or experimentation, any supernatural creature may cause a <i>Deviation</i> in a normal human (and possibly even in a Hunter).<br /> Obs.: this process may result in any <i>Origin</i> or <i>Clade</i>, as normal. That said, <i>Coactives</i> and <i>Mutants</i> are more likely, and while it may be an accident, the obvious presence of a <i>Progenitor</i> makes <i>Pathologicals</i> less common in those cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Questions answered, new question added. 07-21-2025, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T23:30:35-07:00","id":1552351,"title":"","content":"2 and 3 can be found in Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed, in the &quot;Souls of the Sixth Watchtower&quot; sidebar on page 134; slightly more detailed information can be found in each splat's writeup in the &quot;Crossover Considerations&quot; section of the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle, but in short:<br /> <br /> I) Vampires, werewolves, mages, and changelings have souls that can be interacted with through Awakened magic with greater difficulty than mortal/Sleeper souls; hunters have Sleeper souls for the purposes of Awakened magic regardless of what powers they may have developed.<br /> <br /> II) Prometheans, Sin-Eaters/Bound, demons, and Beasts do not have souls that can be interacted with through Awakened magic; the text is contradictory between Beast Core and the PGCC about whether there is any degree of exception allowing powerful Death magic to treat the Horror like a particularly difficult to reach soul, but considering that the Bargain holding a geist in the same metaphysical space for a Sin-Eater is immune and so is a Promethean's proto-soul I defer to the newer material; demons don't have their own souls, but calling in a soul pact makes the &quot;destroyed&quot; soul belong to the demon via the supernatural document, whereupon it can be interacted with through Awakened magic as though it were an Awakened soul.<br /> <br /> III) Mummies and deviants have souls but they cannot be tampered with due to their ownership by the Judges and their tremendous instability, respectively; a deviant with the Dedicated Form from Shallow Graves, which allows the character to have/retain an Integrity rating, loses its benefits in response to attempts to manipulate, destroy, or remove their soul.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why 5 has those two questions in the same line, but Saturnine Night has a whole section from the 1e perspective detailing how any supernatural being might become a demiurge if they avoid using their supernatural powers for the aim, and 2e includes a line in its corebook introduction emphasizing that the strangeness of the Created is such that the printed systems are ultimately no more than tendencies in the long run.<br /> <br /> As far as ghosts go, historically the lines have been very loose about whether or not any sapient creature that isn't a mage or a mortal human can leave a ghost behind, but the 2e mechanics privilege humans with Integrity and objects and animals interacting with such humans when it comes to what does and doesn't create ghosts \u2014 you can magically create a ghost, but the majority of the text doesn't seem to assume ghosts of nonhuman entities to be less than atypical (you might take cues from Geist's observation that necromancers tend to leave geists behind when they die due to the deathly power they held in life, but as brutal as some monsters can be I can't say I'd view blood-soaked vampires and werewolves as equivalent to liches and the lingering obsessions of mortal ritual magicians).<br /> <br /> The answer to 7 is &quot;Yes&quot; for basically all of them due to the fact that even without accounting for sideways applications of their normal energies to produce a Coactive, Cephalists and Mutants are a perpetual source of odd Divergences as traumatic or allergic responses to the supernatural \u2014 much as the Begotten cannot guarantee the nighttime depredations of their Horrors will make more Beasts, the determining factor is in the &quot;material&quot; being acted upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-14-2025, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T00:37:43-07:00","id":1552357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions#post1552345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a few questions I would like to ask, but they're not so simple and I need eleven answers: one for each splat and every splat, even if the answer is obvious. Preferably with reference to books and pages where the answers can be found.<br /> <br /> 1- <i>Do they have normal blood a Vampire can drink? If not, what do they have in its place?</i><br /> 2- <i>Do they have a human Soul? In which state is this Soul?</i><br /> 3- <i>Can their Soul, Soul-like or substitute be removed? Which rules do they follow if Soulless?</i><br /> 4- <i>Do they dream as normal? What difference is there?</i><br /> 5- <i>Can they act as Demiurges? Can they leave Ghosts behind?</i><br /> 6- <i>What would normally be the biggest challenge for a Demon using one of them as Cover?</i><br /> 7- <i>Would it be possible for their regular powers to sometimes produce a Divergence? How?</i><br /> <br /> My plan is to compile the answers in this OP for anyone's future reference:<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire<br /> Werewolf<br /> Mage<br /> Changeling<br /> Promethean<br /> Hunter<br /> Geist<br /> Mummy<br /> Demon<br /> Beast<br /> Deviant</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Number 1 and 2 are addressed in Player guide to Contagion <br /> Number 3 in Mage Nameless and accursed (tremere chapter)<br /> Number 4 in The Hedge (dreaming roads chapter)<br /> <br /> (But I think that copying and pasting the whole text would be against the rules)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T07:29:48-07:00","id":1552367,"title":"","content":"Number 5 (part 2) Do they leave ghosts: is unclear - however from Geist 2e - objects and animals leave ghosts behind by default, the rank of these (castoffs and Barghests) defaults to 0. If a human had an integrity break due to the loss/death/destruction of the entity, it starts at rank 1 instead. If the breaking point fails and the human loses integrity, then it starts at rank 2 (there is no rule for loss which creates multiple breaking points and hurts many humans, but also n\u00f3 rules saying ghosts/Barghest/castoffs can't start at a higher rank).<br /> <br /> So there is an argument for all things leaving behind a ghost. Prometheans/Demons might use the same rules for starting rank as castoffs.<br /> <br /> Geist are already dead, so don't leave another ghost, but are a ghost riding around in their own body (with a Geist for a soul).<br /> <br /> Werewolves, Mages, Hunters, Deviants, and Changelings almost certainly leave ghosts. Probably vampires too. Infact a vampire might leave one ghost when embraced and a second ghost upon final death.<br /> <br /> Mages explicitly leave ghosts, ghost Mage rules have been a thing since 1e. <br /> <br /> As far as I know Mummys can not leave a ghost, can not be killed and will always returns to the service of the Judges. No way out for Mummys they are cursed, I might be wrong about that one.<br /> <br /> Generally, given that lots of things leave ghosts, I think just about everything does. The already dead things (Geist, Mummy, and potentially Vampires) may be exceptions. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T11:45:48-07:00","id":1552382,"title":"","content":"<b>Blood:</b> Werewolves, mages, changelings, demons, beasts, most hunters, and most deviants have physiologically normal blood. The Unnatural Affinity Merit can make these count as satisfying a need from high Blood Potency to drink Kindred blood, excepting most hunters. Promethean blood, Bound blood and mummy blood is likely slightly anomalous, but in a way a vampire feeding wouldn't notice, and the Unnatural Affinity Merit works on them. Vampires have Vitae, which is distinct from ordinary human blood, and forms vitae addiction and the Vinculum when consumed.<br /> <br /> <b>Soul:</b> Most hunters have ordinary human souls. Prometheans, Bound, demons, and beasts do not have souls. Mages have human souls that have linked to the supernal. Mummies have human souls that have been supercharged but chained to greater powers, preventing the soul from being stolen. Deviants have souls that have broken and fissured, and are too unstable to steal. Vampires, werewolves, and changelings have souls, but probably in a state one would not describe as an ordinary human soul. Soullessness has its normal consequences for anyone who normally has a soul and who loses that soul.<br /> <br /> <b>Dream:</b> They all dream. Soulless beings do not have Oneiroi, and their dreams do not connect to the Temenos or Anima Mundi, with the exception of beasts, who fuse with their Horror in their astral Lair when they sleep. Werewolves have inhuman Oneiroi that do not connect to the Temenos.<br /> <br /> <b>Demiurges and ghosts:</b> Everything can act as a demiurge, and everything can leave a ghost, but in the case of Bound and mummies, it would take an extraordinary situation to do so, since they normally survive death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T13:18:43-07:00","id":1552390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions?p=1552382#post1552382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Demiurges and ghosts:</b> Everything can act as a demiurge, and everything can leave a ghost, but in the case of Bound and mummies, it would take an extraordinary situation to do so, since they normally survive death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am pretty sure Mummys survive death better than Bound, but given how dopplegangers are created (and not withstanding what I may have said above) would death for a Mummy not possibly also leave an echo/memory imprint that ghost appear to be composed of?<br /> <br /> And as for the Bound, I think that as ghosts can't leave a ghost neither can this. To reference the Oracle Haunt<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geist2e</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why bother the dead when they\u2019re already one of them? Practitioners of the Oracle are those of the Bound that have realized a single truth \u2014 each and every member of the Bound is dead, meaning they have a perfectly serviceable ghost <br /> ... The Sin-Eater just needs to die. Again. <br /> Each practitioner of the Oracle has their own method of releasing their ghost. ...<br /> No matter the method, the end result is <br /> the same if performed successfully. For a brief moment, the Sin-Eater dies and his ghost is released. ...the Sin-Eater\u2019s ghostly form is barely more than a spectre.</div> </div> </div> </div>The implications here is that they already ARE a ghost, (just one which is usually bound to their body) and thus dying would be the same effect as a ghost dying - ie not leaving another ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T15:46:57-07:00","id":1552393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions?p=1552390#post1552390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am pretty sure Mummys survive death better than Bound, but given how dopplegangers are created (and not withstanding what I may have said above) would death for a Mummy not possibly also leave an echo/memory imprint that ghost appear to be composed of?<br /> <br /> And as for the Bound, I think that as ghosts can't leave a ghost neither can this. To reference the Oracle Haunt<br /> <br /> The implications here is that they already ARE a ghost, (just one which is usually bound to their body) and thus dying would be the same effect as a ghost dying - ie not leaving another ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>My assumption is that mummies and Sin-Eaters usually do not leave ghosts upon their temporary deaths, principally for genre reasons (your ability to die a lot is part of the game and it would be weird if one of the central assumptions of a Geist or Mummy game is that a bunch of leftover you's are going to accumulate and multiply). Diegetically, a ghost appears to be a sort of <i>loss-imprint</i> left behind by a traumatic absence (as per the suggestions that wild animals usually don't leave ghosts, but that beloved pets and otherwise famous or infamous animals are more likely to, similarly with buildings), and one might suppose that if you die and are assured resurrection, your death is less likely to leave a ghost because the trauma is less wrenching and permanent, and thus leaves a shallower imprint.<br /> <br /> I don't leave it out entirely a) because weird shit like doppelgangers happens and it's nice to have room for rare edge cases, and b) a Bound who hits Synergy 0 can die permanently, and the rules section on p. 95 instructs you to discuss with your Storyteller whether your Bound lingers as a ghost. I take this phrasing to suggest that usually the default is no, but the option is left deliberately open for continued play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T01:10:04-07:00","id":1552405,"title":"","content":"I mean, a bound at Synergy 0 dying, while already being a ghost, is not creating a new ghost. <br /> <br /> Which is fine.<br /> <br /> A Mummy has their own relationship with Memory, which, if you look at how memories are made for the Absent, I don't know what to make of it.<br /> <br /> But while traumatic absence is a big part of it. Wild animals *ALL* leave ghosts, they are just rank 0, likely get dragged into the Underworld and walk straight into one of the rivers. So they're not around for long and might aswell not exist.<br /> <br /> Dopplegangers are usually the result of change. Like if the person you were no longer exists, they may leave a ghost behind. A near death experience that leaves you changed is dramatic enough - I think I would allow a Mummy to create a doppleganger in limited circumstances (particularly if they lost Memory and changed being who or what they were...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T06:08:03-07:00","id":1552411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions?p=1552405#post1552405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But while traumatic absence is a big part of it. Wild animals *ALL* leave ghosts, they are just rank 0, likely get dragged into the Underworld and walk straight into one of the rivers. So they're not around for long and might aswell not exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first sentence of the writeup on Barghests in Geist core begins &quot;Most creatures don't leave ghosts&quot; and goes on to explain why before concluding that &quot;a minority&quot; of creatures do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T09:34:26-07:00","id":1552418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions?p=1552382#post1552382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean blood, Bound blood and mummy blood is likely slightly anomalous, but in a way a vampire feeding wouldn't notice,</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that a Promethean doesn't actually have real blood, except maybe one with Sanguine humour, and that drinking their humours would even carry the risk of contamination with Pyros (with potentially explosive consequences, literal or not so).<br /> <br /> But I didn't read any ruling on this, just imagined it from the Promethean Core.<br /> <br /> Unnatural Affinity I'm aware of its effects. Even if a creature doesn't have actual blood, it will make their fluids or fluid-analogous (like Essence) nourishing for the Vampire, and just as much as Vampire blood (for anyone with Blood Potency too high).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T11:14:22-07:00","id":1552420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions?p=1552418#post1552418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was under the impression that a Promethean doesn't actually have real blood, except maybe one with Sanguine humour, and that drinking their humours would even carry the risk of contamination with Pyros (with potentially explosive consequences, literal or not so).<br /> <br /> But I didn't read any ruling on this, just imagined it from the Promethean Core.<br /> <br /> Unnatural Affinity I'm aware of its effects. Even if a creature doesn't have actual blood, it will make their fluids or fluid-analogous (like Essence) nourishing for the Vampire, and just as much as Vampire blood (for anyone with Blood Potency too high).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you use Player guide to Contagion as canon i can assure you that the consequences are quite literally explosive...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T14:18:29-07:00","id":1552428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions?p=1552411#post1552411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first sentence of the writeup on Barghests in Geist core begins &quot;Most creatures don't leave ghosts&quot; and goes on to explain why before concluding that &quot;a minority&quot; of creatures do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is entirely correct. I missed that part, and I don't like it at all.<br /> <br /> For the very same reason I don't like the human centric metaphysics of the setting in general (and absence of human spirits in particular in an animistic sense). But there we are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T07:33:51-07:00","id":1552451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions?p=1552428#post1552428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is entirely correct. I missed that part, and I don't like it at all.<br /> <br /> For the very same reason I don't like the human centric metaphysics of the setting in general (and absence of human spirits in particular in an animistic sense). But there we are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given Chronicles is a fundamentally humanist narrative setting, this just raises questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-21T18:12:54-07:00","id":1552573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions?p=1552451#post1552451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given Chronicles is a fundamentally humanist narrative setting, this just raises questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the setting is fundamentally humanist, it's also fundamentally biased: everything we see, we see from a human perspective.<br /> <br /> Strange things exist all around that can't be explained through any of the splats (when the splats are even capable of explaining themselves). Humans are not deemed particularly important to the universe outside the phenomena they interact with.<br /> <br /> This is far less human centric than WoD ever was. Even for Werewolf(s), while Apocalypse uses the premise that humans aren't that special in the great scheme of things, it always had a problem to adequately explain why every Changing Breed is half human. Forsaken doesn't ever said this is the case, AFAIK, and an animal shapechanger would likely fly under the radar anyway. The sheer amount of unknowns in the setting leaves it to the ST to decide (or not) how much humans are really special, or just too biased (or blind) to notice other things.<br /> <br /> ____________________________________________<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd like to add a new question:<br /> <br /> 8 - <i>How does the splat recovers Willpower (Anchors, sleep, everything)? How frequent and hard should recovery be?</i><br /> <br /> Oh, and I'm going to edit the OP now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-21T20:07:54-07:00","id":1552574,"title":"","content":"I've made the edition. Please look and see if it's everything alright or if something needs tweaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-21T21:41:15-07:00","id":1552577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions?p=1552574#post1552574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've made the edition. Please look and see if it's everything alright or if something needs tweaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making a correction on Demons and Cover: Demons can absolutely get Covers from other demons, whether through transfer pacts, bills of sale, or Cover Trading, all of which are detailed in the Demon supplement <i>Interface</i>, on pages 125-127.<br /> <br /> Cover Trading is simply &quot;demons can make pacts with other demons, though they can only provide each other with Cover elements representing whole dots or whole Covers and they can't provide any other benefits they're be able to give to or as a mortal.&quot; Transfer pacts are made with one party left unspecified to be signed for later, whereas bills of sale are gadgets (created with Academics) that demons can make to change out their name on a pact for that of the demon who signs the bill (though it can't transfer Cover elements that have already been integrated into a Cover).<br /> <br /> General correction on Dreams: With the exception of mages, hunters, Beasts, and deviants, no published non-human non-mortal splat has soul-based access to the Temenos and instead requires outside help approaching it more as another world to be reached with world-hopping powers; vampires in particular are dead while they sleep and their dreams are not restful. Per the Clade Companion, Deviants' access to the Temenos is starkly limited, typically to Realms relating to the means of their Divergence and their Conviction.<br /> <br /> <br /> Re: the new question 8, getting the simple ones out of the way: Hunters, mages, and demons have Virtues and Vices that work like normal humans' do, though demons' Anchors may be unusual in the same way as angels' can and mages may gradually shift their Virtue and/or Vice as their Gnosis increases to reflect their Obsessions and Aspirations (see &quot;Increasing Gnosis,&quot; Mage 2e Core p85-86). Any splat with a Virtue can recover all spent Willpower up to twice per chapter by taking meaningful action in accordance with it, while any splat with a Vice can recover a single point of spent Willpower once per scene by acting in accordance with it to fulfill it. All three splats also dream and recover Willpower from restful sleep. Mages also recover Willpower whenever they get an exceptional success on a spellcasting roll (most easily accomplished with their Praxes), may gain an additional Vice through one of the Conditions brought about by Acts of Hubris, and may directly grant Willpower through moderately powerful Mind spells.<br /> <br /> Deviants have Touchstones tied to their Conviction and Loyalty, which provide a single point of Willpower once per scene spent pursuing the drive or a full refill of Willpower once per chapter when risking danger or suffering in pursuit of the drive; the single-point and full-refill methods are mutually incompatible within the same type of Touchstone and which way they're distributed depends on whether the character is a Renegade or a Devoted; Renegades gain single points of Willpower from pursuing their Conviction Touchstones and full refills from taking risks for their Loyalty Touchstones, while Devoted do the reverse. With certain Merits, they may also have limited access to a Virtue and/or Vice (typically needing to succeed on a Resolve + Composure roll to get the Willpower an act would earn; see the Bleeding Heart and Blood on My Hands Merits on p96 of DtR Core).<br /> <br /> Vampires do not recover Willpower from sleep and must instead rely on their Mask, Dirge, and Touchstones (and, in the case of elders, ritualized behaviors called Anachronisms as described in Thousand Years of Night p18). They may also derive Willpower from the Inspired Condition like any other character, and the Predatory Aura's ability to impose Conditions that lower the exceptional success threshold on certain types of rolls without cost when targeting mortals means they are also incentivized to play toward the Monstrous, Seductive, and/or Competitive Beast (likely taking one of the three mutually-exclusive one-dot Merits that gives one application of the Aura 8-Again while removing 10-Again for the other two).<br /> <br /> Mages, Prometheans, changelings, hunters, mummies, Beasts, and deviants all explicitly or implicitly recover Willpower from a full night's sleep (or seven hours of meditation in the case of the Arisen) in the absence of effects that say otherwise, typically notated in their copy of the core system rules under the section describing the acquisition and/or expenditure of Willpower; Promethean does not have the direct statement that the other lines do, but the Vivid Dreams Merit (PtC2e Core, p117) has an effect on Willpower recovery from rest that doesn't make sense to include in a Promethean-exclusive Merit otherwise.<br /> <br /> Werewolf, Geist, and Demon's corebooks do not explicitly state whether or not their characters recover Willpower from restful sleep, but demons in Cover have human bodies and generally dream (in addition to having Virtues and Vices, as described above). Werewolves are alive, are connected to a dimension of runaway vitality, are ludonarratively the most incentivized to participate in the general system that most eats up Willpower for non-specialists (combat), and dream consistently enough that prophetic dreams are the signature power of one of the five main Auspices (and their default Moon Gift's Sacred Hunt-modifying Facet provides an option that prevents the prey from recovering from rest) in addition to being able to recover single points of Willpower when acting impulsively or rationally in line with their Blood or Bone respectively (increasing to full Willpower recovery if they involve or impede the hunt, submit to Death Rage, cause conflict within their packs, etc.) and likewise gaining single points of Willpower from reinforcing their bonds to one of their two physical and spiritual Touchstones (increasing to full refill if the defense of this relationship put the character's life or pack on the line).<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters can regain one or all of their spent Willpower points from defending their attachment to any of their up-to-three Touchstones (requiring a significant obstacle for one point and serious risk or major cost for the full refill) and from either of their Root and Bloom Anchors (the former from prioritizing the dead over the living, the latter for the opposite; single point once per scene from tending to one community and ignoring the other, full refill once per story from risking your life or status among the opposite community for the corresponding community or protecting one from the other at great risk or cost to yourself), and may also regain one point of Willpower once per scene from participating in an action with their krewe that fulfills its Creed and/or regain all Willpower once per chapter from participating in an action with their krewe that fulfills its Virtue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":"note for Werewolf. 07-22-2025, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T00:42:49-07:00","id":1552578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions?p=1552577#post1552577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making a correction on Demons and Cover: Demons can absolutely get Covers from other demons, whether through transfer pacts, bills of sale, or Cover Trading, all of which are detailed in the Demon supplement <i>Interface</i>, on pages 125-127.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant about the Demon's Cover was that they can't trade in Cover or Cover Parts once those are active Covers, which was my understanding from the Core, so I ask:<br /> <br /> From what you said, it's my understanding that Transfer Pacts and Bills of Sale are &quot;legal&quot; instruments to deal with contracts, but do not alter an already active Cover. Am I right?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I understood that Cover Trading is a contract signed directly between two Demons, dealing in active Covers. Am I correct?<br /> <br /> And finally, the main point is: as far as I understood, a Demon cannot get the demonic identity itself of another as a Cover. That would be the main meaning of &quot;taking a Demon as Cover&quot;.<br /> <br /> If I correctly understood dreams, <b>Vampires</b>, <b>Werewolves</b>, <b>Changelings</b> and <b>Mummies</b> have &quot;normal&quot; Oneiroi and connect to the Anima Mundi, but not to the Temenos? But the others are as I stated (<b>Mages</b>, <b>Hunters </b>and <b>Deviants</b> have normal, human access to the three strata, while <b>Promethean</b>, <b>Geist</b> and <b>Demon</b> have none, and <b>Beast</b> is <b>Beast</b>)?<br /> <br /> However the case, I'll make the corrections at the next major edition. I won't do it right now because I'm nervous about how finicky the forum will get with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T00:57:22-07:00","id":1552579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions?p=1552578#post1552578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I meant about the Demon's Cover was that they can't trade in Cover or Cover Parts once those are active Covers, which was my understanding from the Core, so I ask:<br /> <br /> From what you said, it's my understanding that Transfer Pacts and Bills of Sale are &quot;legal&quot; instruments to deal with contracts, but do not alter an already active Cover. Am I right?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I understood that Cover Trading is a contract signed directly between two Demons, dealing in active Covers. Am I correct?<br /> <br /> And finally, the main point is: as far as I understood, a Demon cannot get the demonic identity itself of another as a Cover. That would be the main meaning of &quot;taking a Demon as Cover&quot;.<br /> <br /> If I correctly understood dreams, <b>Vampires</b>, <b>Werewolves</b>, <b>Changelings</b> and <b>Mummies</b> have &quot;normal&quot; Oneiroi and connect to the Anima Mundi, but not to the Temenos? But the others are as I stated (<b>Mages</b>, <b>Hunters </b>and <b>Deviants</b> have normal, human access to the three strata, while <b>Promethean</b>, <b>Geist</b> and <b>Demon</b> have none, and <b>Beast</b> is <b>Beast</b>)?<br /> <br /> However the case, I'll make the corrections at the next major edition. I won't do it right now because I'm nervous about how finicky the forum will get with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>About dreams, Changeling states that they occour in the Bastions.<br /> Only Mages, Hunters, Deviant and humans have an Oneiroi that reflect their Bastion current dreams.<br /> Other major splats have no Oneiroi, and their dreams are visible ONLY in their Bastions, exept for Beasts who dreams only in their Lairs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T06:56:34-07:00","id":1552585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1552345-basic-splat-interactions?p=1552578#post1552578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what you said, it's my understanding that Transfer Pacts and Bills of Sale are &quot;legal&quot; instruments to deal with contracts, but do not alter an already active Cover. Am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Partially correct; a transfer pact is a normal pact-making option that allows a demon to e.g. make a soul pact and then give the pact to a different demon to call in, and a bill of sale allows a demon to do the same with a pact that they didn't create with that capacity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand, I understood that Cover Trading is a contract signed directly between two Demons, dealing in active Covers. Am I correct? </div> </div> </div>Also correct. Limitations on what they can handle aside, they work the same as ordinary pacts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And finally, the main point is: as far as I understood, a Demon cannot get the demonic identity itself of another as a Cover. That would be the main meaning of &quot;taking a Demon as Cover&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Correct, due to the systems for pacts for Cover involving trading pieces of one's mundane life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I correctly understood dreams, <b>Vampires</b>, <b>Werewolves</b>, <b>Changelings</b> and <b>Mummies</b> have &quot;normal&quot; Oneiroi and connect to the Anima Mundi, but not to the Temenos? But the others are as I stated (<b>Mages</b>, <b>Hunters </b>and <b>Deviants</b> have normal, human access to the three strata, while <b>Promethean</b>, <b>Geist</b> and <b>Demon</b> have none, and <b>Beast</b> is <b>Beast</b>)? </div> </div> </div>It is a general point of lore that the Temenos is not accessible to most &quot;monstrous&quot; splats through the soul due to their having lost or never possessed humanity; this is why deviants have limited access to it (and narratively have the strained dehumanizing relationships that they do with humans, partially mechanized through their Touchstones) and the Begotten have access as semi-natives in a manner closer to the sideways routes used by other monsters specializing their powersets to do so (e.g. demons with the Rip the Gates Exploit or, in 1e, Prometheans with the Crane Athanor introduced in the Astral Realms book).<br /> <br /> It is unconfirmed whether the above psychic &quot;disconnect&quot; still means monsters with souls have Oneiroi, particularly given the typical restrictions mages face on when and where they can meditate into the Astral (with the primary exception, the Astral Adept Merit, only working through the interior of one's own soul), and deviants essentially need the Astral Travel Variation to enter the Astral realms mentally or bodily (and their own souls are more difficult to navigate the more powerful their Scars are). The fact that the Oneiros typically does not practically exist unless it is being experienced by somebody further complicates matters.<br /> <br /> Prometheans access the Azothic Memory as the collective unconscious of all Created, providing them with Elpis visions and basic knowledge of their condition (with Extempore's one-of-a-kind nature requiring them to join an alchemically branded throng of other Prometheans to use powers that tap into Azothic memory), and it may be that other occult frameworks serving as the repository of culture for a given type of monster similarly disconnects their interiority from conventional systems for Astral access to the Oneiros, as deep supernatural trauma and drastic alterations to one's mindset may preclude navigating and altering a mind through metaphorical actions and magical exercises without specialized kit.<br /> <br /> Most splats dream unless stated otherwise in ways that create a Bastion on the Dreaming Roads, per The Hedge (demons being an explicit exception, though the Demon Storyteller's Guide answers the question of whether they dream at all by the &quot;The Labyrinth&quot; item in its Urban Legends chapter, also establishing that even without a soul, being killed in a dream gives them the Harrowed Condition, which is mechanically identical to Soul-Shocked).<br /> <br /> Finally, thematically speaking, anything with a soul (and several things without one that are nevertheless part of the world) has a connection to the Anima Mundi, though the nature of access to the Astral means this doesn't necessarily imply the ability to get there without supernatural assistance like a Primordial Pathway or Rip the Gates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}